   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.05}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The recited amounts do not match: the Grantor is said to pay \"Seventy-five and no/100 Dollars\" yet the figure is written \"$375.00\", and that sum is to buy a $100 face Series E Bond. The word-versus-figure discrepancy is a mechanical error a court could be asked to resolve, though it affects only a nominal corpus.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.06}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The defining clause says \"two (3) certificates\" and then gives both the John Hancock and the Metropolitan certificates the identical number 819800, so the identification of the res is internally erroneous. Because \"Policies of Insurance\" is the operative defined term for the whole trust, a mistake in its identification is capable of being construed.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
 ]},
